{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The consumer matches read readiness by exact `SystemCtx`; it does not treat a newer context as completing older requests. I also traced the backbone gaps: snapshot recovery restores membership before reporting completion, and configuration entries pass through RSM validation before updating Raft membership. That supports a focused read-index correlation Candidate, but not yet a claim of incorrect read values or a timing violation.\n"}}
